The THREE relationships compared side by side:

```java
// ═══ ASSOCIATION: uses — weakest coupling ═══
// TradeService USES MarketDataProvider. Neither owns the other.
// Both exist independently. Injected via Spring.
public class TradeService {
    private final MarketDataProvider marketData;  // USES — association

    public TradeService(MarketDataProvider marketData) {
        this.marketData = marketData;  // INJECTED — not created here
    }

    public BigDecimal getTradeValue(String symbol, int qty) {
        BigDecimal price = marketData.getPrice(symbol);  // USES the association
        return price.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(qty));
    }
}
// UML: TradeService ——→ MarketDataProvider (plain arrow)
// TradeService doesn't CREATE or DESTROY MarketDataProvider.
// Replace MarketDataProvider with another vendor → TradeService doesn't care.

// ═══ AGGREGATION: has — weak ownership ═══
// Portfolio HAS Stocks. Stocks exist independently.
public class Portfolio {
    private final String portfolioId;
    private final List<Stock> stocks = new ArrayList<>();  // HAS stocks

    public void addStock(Stock stock) { stocks.add(stock); }     // stock created OUTSIDE
    public void removeStock(Stock stock) { stocks.remove(stock); } // stock NOT destroyed

    public List<Stock> liquidate() {
        List<Stock> released = new ArrayList<>(stocks);
        stocks.clear();
        return released;  // stocks SURVIVE portfolio liquidation!
    }
}
// UML: Portfolio ◇——→ Stock (hollow diamond)
// Portfolio has stocks but doesn't own their lifecycle.
// Stocks can belong to multiple portfolios (watch list AND holdings).

// ═══ COMPOSITION: owns — strong ownership ═══
// Order OWNS OrderLines. OrderLines are meaningless without the Order.
public class TradeOrder {
    private final String orderId;
    private final List<OrderLine> lines = new ArrayList<>();  // OWNS lines

    public TradeOrder(String orderId) {
        this.orderId = orderId;
    }

    public void addLine(String symbol, int qty, BigDecimal price) {
        lines.add(new OrderLine(orderId + "-L" + (lines.size() + 1), symbol, qty, price));
        // Order CREATES order lines — they are born here
    }

    public void cancel() {
        lines.clear();  // Order lines DESTROYED with order cancellation
        // In JPA: cascade = ALL, orphanRemoval = true
    }

    public List<OrderLine> getLines() { return List.copyOf(lines); }
}
// UML: TradeOrder ◆——→ OrderLine (filled diamond)
// Order creates, manages, and destroys order lines.
// OrderLine without an Order = meaningless (which order? what context?).
```

UML notation visual:

```
  ═══ UML DIAMOND NOTATION ═══

  ASSOCIATION:    TradeService ────────→ MarketDataProvider
                  (plain line with arrow — "uses")

  AGGREGATION:    Portfolio ◇─────────→ Stock
                  (HOLLOW diamond — "has" — part survives)

  COMPOSITION:    TradeOrder ◆─────────→ OrderLine
                  (FILLED diamond — "owns" — part dies with whole)

  Diamond is on the PARENT side (the "whole"):
  ◇ = hollow = weak ownership = aggregation
  ◆ = filled = strong ownership = composition
```

